/-!
# The original symplectic plane family

Exports its meet V1, span V3, generation of L by its literal residuals,
and corrected description by Sylow displacement modulo V1. The resulting
source normalizer control retains only the independent preceding component
uniqueness input. Ordinary Sylow fixed subgroups do not give this plane family.
The L2 point orbit is exactly its Sylow fixed-subgroup family, and both L and
L2 act transitively on their original field-line preimages.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith 11.1.4, printed p.765.
-/
